# Tools/scripts outputs (campaign artifacts, NOT source).
# By default everything in `checkpoints/`, `results/`, `logs/`,
# plus *.json / *.yaml / *.toml is local-only — kept per-evolver,
# never committed.
checkpoints/
logs/
*.yaml
*.toml

# Local evolver state (OpenEvolve database, etc.)
# NOT source — never committed.
.openevolve/
.funsearch/

# Per-campaign scratch artifacts (results/checkpoints/logs are committed
# per PR; these are transient local runs only).
.claude/
*.tmp

# Per-issue committed artifacts (CTF + solar-SIMD + BDF campaigns,
# issues #3337, #3338, #3339) are allow-listed below via `git add -f <file>`
# or by NOT matching the catch-all globs.
# The default catch-all globs `*.json`, `*.yaml`, `*.toml`
# are intentionally narrow:

# Per-edge fixture JSONs (regenerable, source-of-truth).
!edge_cases/

# Per-issue OpenEvolve configs (issue #3337, #3339 et al.).
!configs/

# Per-issue bounded re-run results (issue #3337, #3339 et al.).
!results/

# BDF campaign (#3339) — the seeded orchestration uses these to
# reproduce the byte-equivalent baseline trace and to run the bounded
# re-run documented in `tools/evolution/results/dae/bounded/REPORT.md`.
# The unconditional *.json block above would suppress them, so
# whitelist the schema-v1 Summary JSONs and the campaign log files
# OpenEvolve / the bounded orchestrator emit.
!*.json
!results/dae/
!results/dae/golden/baseline.json
!results/dae/bounded/REPORT.md
!results/dae/bounded/generation_log.jsonl
!results/dae/bounded/summary.json
!results/dae/bounded/winner.json

# OpenEvolve config (issue #3339). The blanket `*.yaml` block
# above suppresses it; whitelist the canonical DAE config.
!configs/dae.yaml
